  "evidence_archive": "ExFiles/Reports/Cpu0857/20261018-final",
  "limits": [
    "BSP PAT is adopted, never rewritten. Supported boot contract requires PAT, MTRRs, PAT0=WB, a strict UC selector, defined effective MTRRs and normal CR0 cache controls; unsupported contracts stop before modules.",
    "The injected readback failure uses a separate ELF and does not claim a physical MSR failure. Normal QEMU APs actually require and confirm PAT synchronization.",
    "UC/WC transitions are limited to confirmed device mappings without cacheable or contradictory aliases. Partial huge-leaf changes are refused unless already WC; no live WB-to-WC conversion is introduced.",
    "MTRRs are read and compared by effective regions, never programmed. Ambiguous overlaps and the cross-vendor WT/WP corner are conservatively refused.",
    "No new native hardware or Windows-host validation, no CPU hotplug. APIC/IRQ/MSI transport ranges remain priority 0.85.8.",
    "Exactly one STANDARD records the final normal artifact; no stable speedup is inferred."
  ]
